The image that docker/Dockerfile.cosmos3-nano builds contains:

- Cosmos3-Nano-Policy-DROID, from NVIDIA Corporation, under the OpenMDW License Agreement, version 1.1
  (OpenMDW-1.1). Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. A copy of the agreement is at
  /opt/cosmos3/LICENSE-OpenMDW-1.1. The model card, with its notices of origin, is README.md in the
  Cosmos3-Nano-Policy-DROID snapshot under /workspace/.cache/huggingface.
- NVIDIA's Cosmos framework code, also under OpenMDW-1.1, in /workspace. Its LICENSE, NOTICE and
  ATTRIBUTIONS.md files are in /workspace.
- The Wan2.2 VAE (Wan2.2_VAE.pth) from Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B, under the Apache License 2.0. A copy of
  the licence is at /opt/cosmos3/LICENSE-Apache-2.0. The model card is README.md in the Wan2.2-TI2V-5B
  snapshot under /workspace/.cache/huggingface.

Positronic packaged these with a serving entry point of its own, server.py, and changed two lines of
NVIDIA's code: the guardrails default is off, and the server announces its roboarena config on
connect. Positronic did not change the model weights.
